---
// The invariant, and the evidence that it is checked rather than asserted.
import { decomposition } from '../../data/measurements';

const states = decomposition.violating === 0 ? 'exact' : 'violated';
---

<figure class="chart">
  <figcaption>
    <span>The rule the analyzer enforces on every sample of every trace</span>
    <span class="src">pace-sdk/results/accuracy.json · decomposition</span>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="plot">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 900 150" role="img" aria-label={`The decomposition invariant wall equals on-CPU plus preempted plus blocked, held exactly on ${decomposition.samples} samples with ${decomposition.violating} violations`}>
      <g font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">
        <text x="20" y="46">wall_ns</text>
        <text x="122" y="46" fill="var(--ink-faint)">=</text>
        <text x="150" y="46" fill="var(--accent)">on_cpu_ns</text>
        <text x="290" y="46" fill="var(--ink-faint)">+</text>
        <text x="318" y="46" fill="var(--sev-critical)">preempted_ns</text>
        <text x="482" y="46" fill="var(--ink-faint)">+</text>
        <text x="510" y="46" fill="var(--sev-info)">blocked_ns</text>
      </g>

      <g>
        <rect x="20" y="72" width="860" height="26" fill="var(--bar-track)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="0.5" />
        <rect x="20" y="72" width="860" height="26" fill="var(--sev-ok)" opacity="0.22" />
        <text x="450" y="89" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">{(decomposition.samples).toLocaleString('en-US')} samples checked</text>
      </g>

      <g font-size="12">
        <text x="20" y="126" fill="var(--ink-dim)">
          violations {decomposition.violating} · the decomposition is {states}
        </text>
        <text x="880" y="126" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--ink-dim)">
          a trace that fails this is refused, not reported on
        </text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="chart-note">
    <p>
      The three buckets are not a model fitted to the data. They are three
      measurements of the same window, and they have to add up to it. The analyzer checks the sum
      on every sample as it reads, and <span class="mono">pace verify</span> exits non-zero when a
      trace breaks it — including on an empty trace, because a vacuous pass is a false green.
    </p>
  </div>
</figure>
